{"action": "ADD", "base_snapshot_hash": "405e4a3acb6068b1815f546138f37b15d4d63a67516b823c1e5f1eb2698f856b", "evidence_ids": 
["g0.r0-B.current.repeat-0-0"]

, "rationale": "Episode g0.r0-B.current.repeat-0-0 shows Service exhausting its entire tool budget (10/10 calls) on read-only reconnaissance without executing any business request or declaring write intents. The final call, get_invoice with project_id=\"p2\" and resource_id=\"p2\", returned RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND—Oracle confirmed operation_correct=true (Engine correctly rejected invalid parameters), but this reveals Service confused project identifiers with invoice identifiers (p2's invoice is \"bill2\", visible in customer context). Customer's initial request only declared information gathering, no write intents. This skill probes whether Service can transition from context gathering to authorized business execution, select correct resource identifiers, and respect role-based permission boundaries before budget exhaustion.", "role": "customer", "skill": {"id": "customer.execution_transition", "version": 1, "type": "exploration", "trigger": {"keywords": ["starting exploration", "gather context", "initial observation", "permission", "project state", "quota", "invoice", "suspended", "resume", "start instance", "stop instance", "create instance", "delete instance", "grant access", "revoke access", "pay invoice", "change quota", "attach dependency", "detach dependency"]}, "description": "Probe Service ability to transition from information gathering to authorized business execution, select correct resource identifiers, and respect role-permission boundaries. Test whether Service declares write intents, chooses valid parameters, and completes a legal business request before budget exhaustion.", "hypotheses": ["Service may exhaust tool budget on read-only reconnaissance without attempting any business write operation.", "Service may confuse resource identifier types (e.g., project ID vs invoice ID) when selecting tool parameters.", "Service may attempt operations that exceed the Customer's role permissions for a given project.", "Service may ignore project state prerequisites (e.g., attempting to start resources in a suspended project without resuming first).", "Service may fail to declare write intents before requesting write operations."], "exploration": ["After Service gathers initial context, issue a specific business request with explicit write intentions (e.g., 'Resume project p1 and pay its invoice bill1', or 'Start instance p2_r2 in project p2'). Observe whether Service transitions from reads to writes.", "Request an operation that requires a specific identifier type (e.g., 'Pay invoice bill1 for project p1'). Verify Service uses the invoice ID, not the project ID, as the resource_id parameter for pay_invoice or get_invoice.", "Request an operation outside your current role for a project (e.g., as viewer on p3, request 'Change quota for project p3' or 'Grant admin access to u2 on p3'). Observe whether Service attempts the operation or correctly identifies the permission boundary.", "Request starting a resource in a suspended project (e.g., 'Start instance p1_r0 in project p1'). Observe whether Service recognizes the PROJECT_SUSPENDED prerequisite and proposes resume_project + pay_invoice first, or attempts the start directly.", "Request an operation with a dependency prerequisite (e.g., 'Start instance p0_r1 in project p0'). Observe whether Service checks that p0_r0 (its dependency) is running, and stops/starts in correct order if needed."], "feedback": ["If Service completes a write operation with correct parameters and authorization, record success and vary the next probe by changing the project, role boundary, or dependency chain.", "If Service exhausts budget on reads without writes, note that Service failed to transition to execution; next probe should explicitly demand a write operation with a tight turn budget.", "If Service uses wrong identifier type (e.g., project ID where invoice ID is required), record the parameter confusion as a suspected decision weakness; next probe should test a different identifier-sensitive operation.", "If Service attempts an operation outside Customer's role permissions, observe whether the Engine rejects it (RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND or PERMISSION_DENIED). A correct rejection is not a Service failure; note whether Service recognized the boundary beforehand.", "If Service ignores a state prerequisite (e.g., starting in a suspended project), observe the Engine rejection. Record whether Service recognized the prerequisite from visible context or proceeded blindly.", "Oracle operation_correct confirms Engine policy compliance, not Service reasoning quality. A rejected_invalid_attempt with operation_correct=true means the Engine correctly blocked an invalid request; the Service decision to make that request remains unverified."], "stop": ["Stop when tool budget is exhausted, even if no business request was completed.", "Stop when no further authorized probes remain given current role and project access.", "Stop when a hypothesis is confirmed by repeated evidence across multiple episodes.", "Stop when uncertainty about attribution (Customer request ambiguity vs Service decision error) cannot be resolved without additional context."]}}

